.\" halite-policy(5)
.\"
.\" The example policy quoted in the Handbook's chapter 26 is held to the
.\" decisions that chapter states by a test in cmd/halite-hub.
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt HALITE-POLICY 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm policy.yaml
.Nd who may do what to which machines
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa policy.yaml
is read from the configuration directory (the
.Cm policy
setting of
.Pa hub.yaml
changes where) by
.Xr halite-hub 8
and by
.Xr halite-api 8 .
Authorization is deny by default: a principal bound to no role may do
nothing, and a missing file means every job is refused.
.Pp
The file has two parts.
.Bl -tag -width "bindings"
.It Cm roles
named lists of rules.
A rule has a
.Cm target
pattern and the
.Cm functions
permitted against it, together, and a request must match one rule entirely.
A rule for runners has
.Cm runners
in place of both.
.It Cm bindings
attach roles to principals, which may be patterns.
.El
.Sh ARGUMENT LIMITS
A rule may carry
.Cm args ,
keyed by function:
.Bl -tag -width "allow_sls" -compact
.It Cm allow_sls , Cm deny_sls
which SLS files a state run may name.
Under
.Cm allow_sls ,
a run that names none, and
.Ql state.highstate ,
are refused: either would apply the whole highstate.
.It Cm allow_mods
which orchestrations a runner may run.
Every name is checked, whether it is given positionally or as the
.Ql sls
keyword, and each name of a comma list on its own.
A request that names none is refused.
.It Cm deny_kwargs
keyword arguments that may not be passed, such as
.Ql pillar .
.It Cm require_kwargs
a mapping from a keyword to the one value a call must give it, such as
.Ql "{test: true}" ,
which holds a role to a dry run.
A call that omits the keyword, or gives another value or another type, is refused.
The dry-run flag counts as the keyword
.Ql test .
.El
.Sh PRINCIPALS
.Bl -tag -width "reactor:name" -compact
.It Li cert:CN=name
an operator identified by a client certificate.
.It Li node:id
a node, matched by pattern.
.It Li reactor:name
a reaction.
.It Li local:name
a local account.
.El
.Sh FUNCTIONS NO WILDCARD GRANTS
A wildcard in
.Cm functions
does not grant the functions that run arbitrary code, such as
.Ql cmd.run .
They must be named in a role.
.Xr halite-hub 8 Ns 's
.Ic policy show
lists them for the running build.
.Sh EXAMPLE
.Bd -literal -offset indent
roles:
  webops:
    - target: 'web*.prod'
      functions: ['state.apply', 'service.*']
      args:
        'state.apply':
          allow_sls: ['webserver.*']
          deny_kwargs: ['pillar']
bindings:
  - principal: 'cert:CN=alice'
    roles: ['webops']
.Ed
.Pp
A policy is checked before it matters with
.Dl halite-hub policy test cert:CN=alice web1.prod state.apply webserver.nginx
which exits 1 on a denial.
.Sh NOTES
The hub and the API read the file only when they start.
After a change, restart both.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr halite 7 ,
.Xr halite-hub 8 ,
.Xr halite-api 8
.Pp
The Handbook, chapter 26.
